# q061 current_customers_by_segment_dataset
# Intent: C5 dataset-path (FROM <gs>) family-B OVER-COUNT TRAP. The `isCurrent true`
#         flag folds into the R2RML pattern's star_constraints; the fused fold has
#         NO star_constraints handling, so it MUST decline (the O1 guard) and
#         materialize the CONSTRAINED count. The blessed oracle is the current-only
#         count; a silent fuse would over-count (ALL customers) and fail this member.
# BI lineage (BI-13): "How are current customers distributed across segments?"
# Predicates verified against enterprise.ttl — DimCustomer: isCurrent, segment.
# Exec path: query_from() with FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main> (the deployed solo shape).
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?seg (COUNT(?c) AS ?n)
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?c a edw:Customer ; edw:isCurrent true ; edw:segment ?seg . }
GROUP BY ?seg
